<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Completion graph caching, family G: many independent ABox groups.

  Twelve groups of two individuals a_i, b_i that are both an r-predecessor of
  their own o_i, where o_i has at most one r-predecessor. Every pair has to be
  merged in the consistency test, but the groups are independent, so the ABox
  is processed in several saturation rounds / with many representative
  neighbours. The tests touch one pair at a time; a test that merges the test
  node with {a_5} must reactivate b_5 and re-derive the merge, but not the
  other groups. Group 1 additionally has the disjunction in the t-successor of
  a_1, so the cached model differs from the deterministic graph.
-->
